      "css": ".ds-band{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto minmax(0,1fr) auto;align-items:center;gap:18px;width:100%;padding:12px 36px;border:0;background:var(--band,#18171b);color:#fff;text-align:left;cursor:pointer}.ds-band-l{padding:3px 8px;background:var(--due,#f5c400);color:var(--on-due,#2b2100);font-family:var(--font-condensed),\"Sofia Sans Condensed\",\"Arial Narrow\",sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase}.ds-band-t{font-weight:650;font-size:16px}.ds-band-t small{font-size:13px;font-weight:400;opacity:.8;margin-left:12px}.ds-band:hover .ds-band-t{text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:var(--due,#f5c400)}.ds-band:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--due,#f5c400);outline-offset:-4px}.ds-band-c{font-family:var(--font-condensed),\"Sofia Sans Condensed\",\"Arial Narrow\",sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:22px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-band-c small{font-size:14px;font-weight:600;margin-right:6px;opacity:.8}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Answer Sheet",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Answer Sheet\"**\n\nDueCare is still drawn like a printed answer sheet: white stock, ruled lines, condensed printed labels and square boxes. Rose drop-out ink prints the structure the institution owns (field and column labels, timetable slot outlines, hour rules, the now line). Graphite carries the student's text and actions. On top of those two inks sits one more layer the owner asked for directly: status colour. Completed is green, due is yellow, overdue is solid red, and missed is red tint with the title struck through. That colour appears only where a deadline's state is shown, so a glance at the week answers \"what's done, what's due, what's late\".\n\nThe interface is meant to be simple to move around. One header row holds the wordmark, five plain text tabs, the bell, Add task and the account button. The week sheet reads top to bottom: day heads, a \"Due\" row listing each day's deadlines in plain words, then a timeline of classes with the now line. There are no shadows and no rounded rectangles. Depth comes from 1px rules and solid fills.\n\nDark mode is a carbon sheet. The paper turns near-black, rose brightens to #ff6f9c, graphite becomes the light ink, and each status colour has its own dark value. The next-due band stays a dark strip (#2b262d) in both modes.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Rose prints structure, graphite carries text and action, and green, yellow and red show status only.",
      "One-row header with plain text tabs and a 4px graphite underline on the active tab.",
      "Square corners everywhere. The oval bubble is the only curve.",
      "No shadows. Depth comes from 1px rules and solid fills.",
      "Condensed face for labels and numerals, Sofia Sans for reading, tabular numerals for every time and count."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Status Colour Rule",
        "body": "Completed is green, due is yellow, overdue is solid red, missed is red tint with strike-through (owner commitment). These colours appear wherever a deadline's state is shown (status pills, due items, month chips, summary counts, day ticks, review badges) and nowhere else. They are never used for structure, decoration or buttons.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two-Ink Rule",
        "body": "Outside status, a fill is sheet, a rose density, or graphite. Rose prints structure and graphite carries text and action. No neutral grey surface exists.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hatch Rule",
        "body": "Anything waiting for the student's review, and any day outside the current month, takes the diagonal \"do not write\" hatch (-45deg, Rose Tint 2px every 7px). This covers the attention banner, import rows that need a fix, and outside days in the month view.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Printed Caps Rule",
        "body": "Uppercase condensed caps are reserved for labels the sheet itself would print: a field name, a day name, a row label, a status, or a priority flag. They label data that sits right next to them. They never sit above a heading as a decorative eyebrow.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Every time, date and count uses `tabular-nums`.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No-Shadow Rule",
        "body": "`box-shadow` and `text-shadow` are banned (owner commitment). If something needs to lift, give it a heavier rule or a solid fill instead.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Curve Rule",
        "body": "Rounded corners are banned (owner commitment). Only the bubble curves. It is either empty with a rose stroke, filled graphite for a selection, or filled with the item's status colour on a due item.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** colour every deadline state the same way everywhere: green completed, yellow due, solid red overdue, red tint with strike-through missed (the Status Colour Rule).",
      "**Do** keep every non-status surface sheet white, a rose density, or graphite.",
      "**Do** use 1px Rose Rule for internal divisions and 1px graphite for the outer frame of a working sheet.",
      "**Do** write state in plain words next to its colour (\"done\", \"overdue\", \"missed\"), so colour is never the only signal.",
      "**Do** set every time, date and count in Sofia Sans Condensed with tabular numerals.",
      "**Do** mark review-pending items with the -45deg Rose Tint hatch.",
      "**Do** keep targets at 44px or taller and the focus outline at 2px graphite.",
      "**Do** use the house easing cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1) at 160 to 300ms, and drop all motion under prefers-reduced-motion."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use drop shadows or text shadows anywhere (owner commitment).",
      "**Don't** round corners. Radius is 0 everywhere except the oval bubble (owner commitment).",
      "**Don't** use green, yellow or red for anything that isn't a deadline's state: no coloured buttons, headers or decoration.",
      "**Don't** introduce neutral grey surfaces or hues beyond rose, graphite and the three status colours.",
      "**Don't** put caps above a heading as a decorative eyebrow. Printed caps label data, not sections.",
      "**Don't** add a second navigation row or boxed header fields. The header is one row.",
      "**Don't** build the sidebar + KPI-card + chart dashboard. Information sits on the sheet, in ruled boxes."
    ]
  }
}
